# Unsure: S2 gives the meaning of the word "God", so "infinite goodness" there is most naturally limitless perfection. S1's principle needs "infinite" to mean a contrary that occupies all reality and so destroys its opposite. A God of unlimited perfection could exist while evil exists elsewhere. So P2 could be true and the antecedent P1 needs false.
# No bridge: the shift sits inside the shared claim itself, not in a premise or assumption that joins two claims.
